From 0cdd58549405cde1ef4a686b02e97425b533eb57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 03:45:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the ontology-ci pre-push hook able to fail, and stop it
 discarding the artifact make ci rebuilt

The `ontology-ci` hook had two defects that both presented as a green run.

It could not fail. The `entry` chain ended `git checkout --
docs/webvowl/data/ontology.json || true`, and a shell returns the status of
the last command in the list, so the hook returned that trailing `|| true`
and exited 0 for every build. Measured against a deliberately broken
ontology (a `gcdfo:` class with no `gcdfo:theme`, which trips
`theme-coverage`): `make ci` exits 2 and the hook reported `Passed`, exit 0.
The gate had never failed for anybody since it was introduced.

It discarded a build product. `make ci` regenerates
`docs/webvowl/data/ontology.json` -- the path is inside `CI_ARTIFACT_PATHS`
-- and `.github/workflows/ci.yml` rejects any uncommitted change left after
`make ci`. The hook's `files` pattern restricts it to changes to
`ontology/dfo-salmon.ttl`, which is exactly when that artifact is expected
to change, so the hook threw away locally what CI then demanded and left the
tree with three regenerated docs artifacts and one reset to HEAD.

The fix captures the build's status in `ci_status`, runs the restore only on
the failure path, and exits with `ci_status`. The failure-path restore is
kept deliberately: `docs-widoco` rsyncs raw WIDOCO output over that path
before the normalizer runs, so a build that dies in between leaves raw
generator bytes a later run would adopt as its normalizer baseline and go
green over. Restoring on failure is the remedy `docs/tech-debt.md`
prescribes under its 2026-08-16 entry, which says to run it before retrying
a FAILED docs build rather than after every push -- so this half needed no
wait on that entry's own fix.

The comment block on the hook carries both rules and the retirement
condition for the failure branch: it goes when the 2026-08-16 tech-debt
entry retires, because that fix makes `docs-widoco` restore the pre-run
bytes itself and leaves nothing for the branch to do.

Evidence, all against the same deliberately broken ontology or the same
label edit:
  - broken ontology, before: `Passed`, pre-commit exit 0
  - broken ontology, after:  `Failed`, `exit code: 2`, pre-commit exit 1
  - valid ontology edit, before: `docs/webvowl/data/ontology.json` absent
    from the post-hook tree
  - valid ontology edit, after:  present, and `make ci-sync-artifacts`
    stages all four artifacts
  - clean valid tree, after: `Passed`, exit 0, tree untouched
  - dirtied `ontology.json` plus a failing build, after: restored, and the
    hook still exits 2

Refs hub queue item B-150.
---
 .pre-commit-config.yaml | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.pre-commit-config.yaml b/.pre-commit-config.yaml
index e0acbc7..85cd3a1 100644
--- a/.pre-commit-config.yaml
+++ b/.pre-commit-config.yaml
@@ -1,17 +1,49 @@
 repos:
   - repo: local
     hooks:
+      # Runs the full CI bundle before a push that touches the canonical
+      # ontology, so a push cannot introduce what `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
+      # would reject anyway.
+      #
+      # Two properties of the `entry` below are load-bearing. Both were absent
+      # until 2026-09-16 and neither failure was visible from reading a green
+      # run, so change the chain only with the reasoning here in hand.
+      #
+      # 1. THE BUILD'S EXIT STATUS IS THE HOOK'S EXIT STATUS. The chain used to
+      #    end `git checkout -- docs/webvowl/data/ontology.json || true`, and a
+      #    shell returns the status of the last command in the list, so the hook
+      #    returned that `|| true` and exited 0 for every build — including
+      #    failing ones. The gate had therefore never failed for anybody since
+      #    it was introduced. `ci_status` is captured immediately after the
+      #    build and is what this entry exits with; do not end the chain with a
+      #    command whose status is not the build's. The same fault, and the same
+      #    rule, are recorded on `ci-sync-artifacts` in the Makefile.
+      #
+      # 2. THE `git checkout` RUNS ONLY WHEN THE BUILD FAILED. `make ci`
+      #    regenerates `docs/webvowl/data/ontology.json` (it is inside
+      #    `CI_ARTIFACT_PATHS`), and CI rejects any uncommitted change left
+      #    after `make ci` across the whole worktree. Discarding that file after
+      #    a SUCCESSFUL build threw away the very artifact CI then demanded, and
+      #    left the tree holding three regenerated docs artifacts and one reset
+      #    to HEAD. After a FAILED build the restore is still wanted, for a
+      #    different reason: `docs-widoco` rsyncs raw WIDOCO output over that
+      #    path before the normalizer runs, so a build that dies in between
+      #    leaves raw generator bytes that the next run would adopt as its
+      #    normalizer baseline and go green over. Restoring on failure is
+      #    exactly the remedy `docs/tech-debt.md` prescribes under
+      #    "2026-08-16 — A failed `make docs-widoco` can re-baseline WebVOWL
+      #    output to raw generator bytes", which says to run it before retrying
+      #    a FAILED docs build — not after every push.
+      #
+      # Retires when: that 2026-08-16 tech-debt entry retires. Its fix makes
+      #    `docs-widoco` restore the pre-run bytes itself on failure, at which
+      #    point the failure branch below has nothing left to do and it, and
+      #    this note, are deleted rather than left as a second restorer.
       - id: ontology-ci
         name: Run full ontology CI bundle (make ci)
-        entry: bash -lc 'if [ -z "${JAVA_HOME:-}" ]; then if [ -d /usr/local/opt/openjdk@17/libexec/openjdk.jdk/Contents/Home ]; then export JAVA_HOME=/usr/local/opt/openjdk@17/libexec/openjdk.jdk/Contents/Home; export PATH="$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH"; elif command -v /usr/libexec/java_home >/dev/null 2>&1; then export JAVA_HOME=$(/usr/libexec/java_home -v 17 2>/dev/null || true); [ -n "${JAVA_HOME:-}" ] && export PATH="$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH"; fi; fi; if command -v devenv >/dev/null 2>&1; then devenv shell make ci; else make ci; fi; git checkout -- docs/webvowl/data/ontology.json || true'
+        entry: bash -lc 'if [ -z "${JAVA_HOME:-}" ]; then if [ -d /usr/local/opt/openjdk@17/libexec/openjdk.jdk/Contents/Home ]; then export JAVA_HOME=/usr/local/opt/openjdk@17/libexec/openjdk.jdk/Contents/Home; export PATH="$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH"; elif command -v /usr/libexec/java_home >/dev/null 2>&1; then export JAVA_HOME=$(/usr/libexec/java_home -v 17 2>/dev/null || true); [ -n "${JAVA_HOME:-}" ] && export PATH="$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH"; fi; fi; if command -v devenv >/dev/null 2>&1; then devenv shell make ci; else make ci; fi; ci_status=$?; if [ "$ci_status" -ne 0 ]; then git checkout -- docs/webvowl/data/ontology.json; fi; exit "$ci_status"'
         language: system
         files: ^ontology/dfo-salmon\.ttl$
         pass_filenames: false
         always_run: false
         stages: [pre-push, manual]
